;;; The twin of `wild-in-absent.ein` — M1e2 **W20**, banked by S1e2.2.20
;;; (2026-11-05): the same program with the wildcard `_` written as `?any`, a
;;; variable the rule reads nowhere else, which under `absent` asks after any
;;; `holds` fact at all. Its answer is the witness's right one: `z` never
;;; fires, and R is `∅` and `{(hit a)}` (`ein solve FILE` at `c73a0796`,
;;; release and debug).

(relation holds Node) (relation hit Node)
(holds a)
(rule z () :match (absent (holds ?any)) :assert (hit z))
(solve :no-hypothesis (holds))
